    "review_depth": "Read the University of Warwick author-accepted manuscript for the original abstract, methods, call-combination criteria, MCA/results, proposed interpretations and stated limitations. Read the full PeerJ critique in PMC, including its null simulations, dependence argument, full-pipeline permutation reanalysis, discussion and data/code availability. The original abstract describes 700 calls/call combinations; the critique describes 735 repeated observations. Acquired only the separately released Figshare v1 xdata.txt input through the bounded collector; its 801,667 bytes matched provider MD5 24bcbb0c1b4d98ad645168307cb4f500, and the receipt records SHA-256 84ad7b48bb41cf55b4f92c5a2fcf57780ad5590b0b4d941684f3a843b1abd6a4. A row-value-free structural check found 735 tab-delimited data rows, 343 unique columns and the expected seven leading metadata columns plus 336 feature columns, matching the pinned scripts' input layout. The file's individual/group headings were not used to emit any row values. The Figshare workbook was not acquired. The Zenodo code archive was checksum-verified transiently; README and all three scripts at pinned commit b918fd2e03379c1d1d4abca51eca21de41ce5ec6 were reviewed. Script 03 sets nperm=100 although the paper reports 10,000 permutations. No code was executed, dependencies installed or outputs reproduced; no original authors' response was reviewed.",
    "finding": "Berthet et al. (2025) used more than 300 contextual features, Multiple Correspondence Analysis and geometric criteria to argue that four bonobo call combinations were compositional, including three non-trivial combinations. Wartel et al. (2026) challenge the inferential pipeline: their simulations report 34.5–84.3% significant outcomes under null conditions depending on missingness handling, and their alternative procedure recomputes the full MCA within 10,000 permutations and reports p=0.2597. The critique's Zenodo code archive omits the xdata.txt input, but the original study's separately released Figshare v1 file has a checksum-verified 735-by-343 tabular layout and the metadata-column positions expected by the pinned scripts. This matches the critique's reported 735 observations and script dimensions; it does not resolve the original abstract's 700-count discrepancy or prove the data/code version was used for the published result. The weighted-MCA script uses 100 permutations, so it cannot yield the reported four-decimal p-value as written. Its script also calculates observation weights from original call labels, then reassigns labels while retaining those weights; whether this is the intended null weighting needs specialist review. Talk2Nature has not reproduced or adjudicated the statistical result. This remains a peer-reviewed methodological dispute, not evidence that bonobos lack communication or that the scientific question is settled.",
    "limitations": "The original work studies wild bonobo vocal and contextual observations; it is not a machine-learning translation system or a receiver-comprehension experiment. The critique's null simulations and alternative test are published reanalysis results, not a Talk2Nature reproduction. Its conclusion depends on the critique's proposed null/permutation design; we have not reviewed a response from the original authors or independently adjudicated the competing statistical arguments. The source table contains 735 data rows, matching the critique, while the original abstract states 700; that publication-level difference remains unresolved. The Zenodo release declares CC BY 4.0 for its code archive, and the Figshare v1 item declares CC BY 4.0 for the data item; component terms are not transferred between them. Only xdata.txt was retained in ignored local external storage for a bounded structural audit; no row values are in Git, the website or report. The GitHub code repository has no recognized LICENSE, and the original accepted manuscript's repository notice prohibits redistribution. No code, dependencies, audio or workbook were executed/acquired; no result was reproduced.",
    "lesson": "For Talk2Nature, keep representation geometry and exploratory clusters separate from confirmatory evidence of meaning. Before testing context structure, define a biologically motivated feature set and hypothesis; preserve individual, session and observation dependence; report call counts, missingness and sampling imbalance; and construct null tests that repeat the entire data-dependent representation and analysis pipeline. Freeze and checksum every required input and code release, pin the software environment, and verify that the executable settings match the paper's reported settings before claiming reproducibility. Compare against simple and context-only baselines, and use receiver behavior or another independent outcome when the claim concerns comprehension. An embedding or fluent model caption alone cannot establish semantics.",
