    "lesson": "Keep Talk2Nature multi-species in scope, but define one species-specific question at a time. For any future dog task, first compare a simple acoustic baseline, a general bioacoustic representation and a dog-specific representation on an independently grouped, rights-cleared test; report event detection separately from bark-category labels and never call either translation. The large web-sourced corpus is not a shortcut around provenance or rights review. This does not establish that dogs should replace parrots as the first usability cohort: choose that cohort based on an accessible, repeatable passive-observation question and a responsible study path, not on scraped-hour totals.",
